From 04808b222ec7d6d4b3f4c226e7fd32370b0b330e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:07:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban blocker probe lane: recheck routes of an open
 provider-scoped blocker on a 300 s cadence (G2 follow-up)

Follow-up to PR #2677 (G2), exact-head review 5898596145 (card t_01a1d6ea60f68015).

Defect: the G2 gate on `dispatch.shared_blocker_probed` keys on the board content revision, this gateway's id and
the main config signature. For a provider-scoped blocker, `probe_stranded_blockers` decides which cards behind it
count through `task_applies -> task_route`, which also reads inputs outside that key: the assignee profile's
config.yaml (`_assignee_config`), the effective user/managed config (`class_unroutable_reason`), provider walls and
quota episodes that end with time. When a blocked card's route moved into the blocker's scope with no board write,
`ids` was empty, nothing was appended to `due_out`, and the lane stayed skipped until the next content write or the
14-day lookback exit: unbounded on a quiet board.

Fix: while a provider-scoped blocker is open with cards behind it, the probe lane appends
`now + ROUTE_RECHECK_SECONDS` (300 s) to its due times. A bounded cadence instead of a fingerprint because the
route's inputs include clocks (wall/episode expiry) that no file signature captures. Unscoped blockers are
unchanged (their scope never reads routes).

Proof:
- RED -> GREEN: test_scoped_blocker_probe_reruns_when_a_route_enters_its_scope_with_no_board_write fails on
  62dd71093e (`assert [] == ['t_...']`: the lane stays gated after the assignee route flips with the revision
  unchanged) and passes here; the same test shows the lane is still skipped one tick later with nothing moved.
- test_unscoped_blocker_adds_no_route_recheck pins the scope condition.
- Mutants killed: drop `st.blocker_provider` (2 sweep_gate tests fail); drop `due_out is not None`
  (test_stranded_probe_ignores_other_provider_running fails); drop the append (the RED above).
- test_kanban_sweep_gate, test_kanban_shared_blockers, test_kanban_ci_progress: 160 passed.
- scripts/check --only health: ok.

Budget (hub `default` board copy, 2026-11-13 22:05 UTC; scripts/kanban_reclaim_replay_bench.py, 120 ticks):
- replay 1800 s (100 write ticks): 62dd71093e 48.0 ms/tick (0.32% of a core) vs this head 50.8 ms (0.34%);
  write-free: 24.5 vs 24.7 ms (0.16%). The board has no blocked card now, so the probe lane does not run in either;
  the difference is run noise.
- Cadence cost, upper bound measured on the same copy: blocker_states 11.6 ms + task_route for 50 cards 110.5 ms
  = 122 ms per recheck; at one recheck per 300 s that is 0.04% of a core, only while a provider-scoped blocker is
  open with cards behind it.
